window.__READMES["sagrag"]="<div id=\"readme\" class=\"md\" data-path=\"README.md\"><article class=\"markdown-body entry-content container-lg\" itemprop=\"text\"><div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h1 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">SAG-RAG</h1><a id=\"user-content-sag-rag\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: SAG-RAG\" href=\"#sag-rag\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Speculative -&gt; Agentic -&gt; Graph RAG: retrieval-augmented question answering\nover your own documents. SAG-RAG plans the search, runs semantic and keyword\nretrieval in parallel, reranks the passages, optionally consults a knowledge\ngraph, has the evidence judged, and writes an answer whose citations point at\nexact character spans in the source files. It ships as a FastAPI backend over\nQdrant, Elasticsearch, Neo4j and a local Ollama model, with a web UI,\nPrometheus/Grafana observability, and optional API-key multi-tenancy.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Docs:</strong> component and data-flow reference in <a href=\"docs/architecture.md\"><code>docs/architecture.md</code></a>.\nWith the backend running, the live API schema is at <strong><code>/docs</code></strong> (Swagger UI)\nand <strong><code>/redoc</code></strong>.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Architecture</h2><a id=\"user-content-architecture\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Architecture\" href=\"#architecture\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<section class=\"js-render-needs-enrichment render-needs-enrichment position-relative\" data-identity=\"2c01c32a-5687-457f-85e6-7efb62f84e04\" data-host=\"https://viewscreen.githubusercontent.com\" data-src=\"https://viewscreen.githubusercontent.com/markdown/mermaid?docs_host=https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.github.com\" data-type=\"mermaid\" aria-label=\"mermaid rendered output container\">\n  <div class=\"js-render-enrichment-target\" data-json=\"{&quot;data&quot;:&quot;---\\nconfig:\\n  look: neo\\n  theme: redux\\n---\\nflowchart LR\\n\\n  subgraph A[1. Request and Planning]\\n    direction TB\\n    UI[Web UI]\\n    API[FastAPI /v1/query]\\n    PLAN[Speculative Planner]\\n    ROUTE[Domain Router]\\n    LLM[Ollama LLM]\\n    UI --&gt; API\\n    API --&gt; PLAN\\n    PLAN --&gt; ROUTE\\n    PLAN --&gt; LLM\\n  end\\n\\n  subgraph B[2. Retrieval Layer]\\n    direction TB\\n    RETR[Retrieval Fanout]\\n    VEC[Vector Search\\\\nQdrant]\\n    LEX[Lexical Search\\\\nElasticsearch]\\n    STR[Structured Lines\\\\nfrom lexical hits]\\n    AUTH[Author Lexical Search\\\\nConditional ES source keyword]\\n    RETR --&gt; VEC\\n    RETR --&gt; LEX\\n    LEX --&gt; STR\\n  end\\n\\n  subgraph C[3. Evidence Processing]\\n    direction TB\\n    AGG[Aggregate + Normalize]\\n    POL[Policy + Freshness Filters]\\n    DEDUP[Deduplicate Evidence]\\n    BIAS[Author Bias\\\\nsoft-strong]\\n    RR[Re-ranker\\\\nCross-Encoder]\\n    AGG --&gt; POL --&gt; DEDUP --&gt; BIAS --&gt; RR\\n  end\\n\\n  subgraph D[4. Optional Graph Reasoning]\\n    direction TB\\n    G[Knowledge Graph\\\\nNeo4j]\\n    J[Judge / Contradictions]\\n    G --&gt; J\\n  end\\n\\n  subgraph E[5. Synthesis and Output]\\n    direction TB\\n    SYN[Synthesis and Fallback\\\\nnon_json timeout error]\\n    OUT[Answer + Provenance + Scores]\\n    SYN --&gt; OUT\\n  end\\n\\n  subgraph F[6. Telemetry]\\n    direction TB\\n    OBS[Metrics + Diagnostics]\\n    RF[retrieval_failures]\\n    AD[agent_diagnostics]\\n    SM[synthesis outcomes + latency]\\n    OBS --&gt; RF\\n    OBS --&gt; AD\\n    OBS --&gt; SM\\n  end\\n\\n  subgraph G2[7. Ingestion Pipeline]\\n    direction TB\\n    DOCS[Docs]\\n    CHUNK[Chunk + Embed]\\n    ES[Elasticsearch Index]\\n    QDR[Qdrant Vectors]\\n    NEO[Neo4j Graph]\\n    DOCS --&gt; CHUNK\\n    CHUNK --&gt; ES\\n    CHUNK --&gt; QDR\\n    CHUNK --&gt; NEO\\n  end\\n\\n  ROUTE --&gt; RETR\\n  API -. explicit author terms .-&gt; AUTH\\n  VEC --&gt; AGG\\n  LEX --&gt; AGG\\n  STR --&gt; AGG\\n  AUTH --&gt; AGG\\n  RR --&gt; SYN\\n  SYN --&gt; LLM\\n  RR -.-&gt; G\\n  J -.-&gt; SYN\\n  J -.-&gt; LLM\\n  OUT --&gt; OBS\\n&quot;}\" data-plain=\"---\nconfig:\n  look: neo\n  theme: redux\n---\nflowchart LR\n\n  subgraph A[1. Request and Planning]\n    direction TB\n    UI[Web UI]\n    API[FastAPI /v1/query]\n    PLAN[Speculative Planner]\n    ROUTE[Domain Router]\n    LLM[Ollama LLM]\n    UI --&gt; API\n    API --&gt; PLAN\n    PLAN --&gt; ROUTE\n    PLAN --&gt; LLM\n  end\n\n  subgraph B[2. Retrieval Layer]\n    direction TB\n    RETR[Retrieval Fanout]\n    VEC[Vector Search\\nQdrant]\n    LEX[Lexical Search\\nElasticsearch]\n    STR[Structured Lines\\nfrom lexical hits]\n    AUTH[Author Lexical Search\\nConditional ES source keyword]\n    RETR --&gt; VEC\n    RETR --&gt; LEX\n    LEX --&gt; STR\n  end\n\n  subgraph C[3. Evidence Processing]\n    direction TB\n    AGG[Aggregate + Normalize]\n    POL[Policy + Freshness Filters]\n    DEDUP[Deduplicate Evidence]\n    BIAS[Author Bias\\nsoft-strong]\n    RR[Re-ranker\\nCross-Encoder]\n    AGG --&gt; POL --&gt; DEDUP --&gt; BIAS --&gt; RR\n  end\n\n  subgraph D[4. Optional Graph Reasoning]\n    direction TB\n    G[Knowledge Graph\\nNeo4j]\n    J[Judge / Contradictions]\n    G --&gt; J\n  end\n\n  subgraph E[5. Synthesis and Output]\n    direction TB\n    SYN[Synthesis and Fallback\\nnon_json timeout error]\n    OUT[Answer + Provenance + Scores]\n    SYN --&gt; OUT\n  end\n\n  subgraph F[6. Telemetry]\n    direction TB\n    OBS[Metrics + Diagnostics]\n    RF[retrieval_failures]\n    AD[agent_diagnostics]\n    SM[synthesis outcomes + latency]\n    OBS --&gt; RF\n    OBS --&gt; AD\n    OBS --&gt; SM\n  end\n\n  subgraph G2[7. Ingestion Pipeline]\n    direction TB\n    DOCS[Docs]\n    CHUNK[Chunk + Embed]\n    ES[Elasticsearch Index]\n    QDR[Qdrant Vectors]\n    NEO[Neo4j Graph]\n    DOCS --&gt; CHUNK\n    CHUNK --&gt; ES\n    CHUNK --&gt; QDR\n    CHUNK --&gt; NEO\n  end\n\n  ROUTE --&gt; RETR\n  API -. explicit author terms .-&gt; AUTH\n  VEC --&gt; AGG\n  LEX --&gt; AGG\n  STR --&gt; AGG\n  AUTH --&gt; AGG\n  RR --&gt; SYN\n  SYN --&gt; LLM\n  RR -.-&gt; G\n  J -.-&gt; SYN\n  J -.-&gt; LLM\n  OUT --&gt; OBS\n\" dir=\"auto\">\n    <div class=\"render-plaintext-hidden\" dir=\"auto\">\n      <pre lang=\"mermaid\" aria-label=\"Raw mermaid code\">---\nconfig:\n  look: neo\n  theme: redux\n---\nflowchart LR\n\n  subgraph A[1. Request and Planning]\n    direction TB\n    UI[Web UI]\n    API[FastAPI /v1/query]\n    PLAN[Speculative Planner]\n    ROUTE[Domain Router]\n    LLM[Ollama LLM]\n    UI --&gt; API\n    API --&gt; PLAN\n    PLAN --&gt; ROUTE\n    PLAN --&gt; LLM\n  end\n\n  subgraph B[2. Retrieval Layer]\n    direction TB\n    RETR[Retrieval Fanout]\n    VEC[Vector Search\\nQdrant]\n    LEX[Lexical Search\\nElasticsearch]\n    STR[Structured Lines\\nfrom lexical hits]\n    AUTH[Author Lexical Search\\nConditional ES source keyword]\n    RETR --&gt; VEC\n    RETR --&gt; LEX\n    LEX --&gt; STR\n  end\n\n  subgraph C[3. Evidence Processing]\n    direction TB\n    AGG[Aggregate + Normalize]\n    POL[Policy + Freshness Filters]\n    DEDUP[Deduplicate Evidence]\n    BIAS[Author Bias\\nsoft-strong]\n    RR[Re-ranker\\nCross-Encoder]\n    AGG --&gt; POL --&gt; DEDUP --&gt; BIAS --&gt; RR\n  end\n\n  subgraph D[4. Optional Graph Reasoning]\n    direction TB\n    G[Knowledge Graph\\nNeo4j]\n    J[Judge / Contradictions]\n    G --&gt; J\n  end\n\n  subgraph E[5. Synthesis and Output]\n    direction TB\n    SYN[Synthesis and Fallback\\nnon_json timeout error]\n    OUT[Answer + Provenance + Scores]\n    SYN --&gt; OUT\n  end\n\n  subgraph F[6. Telemetry]\n    direction TB\n    OBS[Metrics + Diagnostics]\n    RF[retrieval_failures]\n    AD[agent_diagnostics]\n    SM[synthesis outcomes + latency]\n    OBS --&gt; RF\n    OBS --&gt; AD\n    OBS --&gt; SM\n  end\n\n  subgraph G2[7. Ingestion Pipeline]\n    direction TB\n    DOCS[Docs]\n    CHUNK[Chunk + Embed]\n    ES[Elasticsearch Index]\n    QDR[Qdrant Vectors]\n    NEO[Neo4j Graph]\n    DOCS --&gt; CHUNK\n    CHUNK --&gt; ES\n    CHUNK --&gt; QDR\n    CHUNK --&gt; NEO\n  end\n\n  ROUTE --&gt; RETR\n  API -. explicit author terms .-&gt; AUTH\n  VEC --&gt; AGG\n  LEX --&gt; AGG\n  STR --&gt; AGG\n  AUTH --&gt; AGG\n  RR --&gt; SYN\n  SYN --&gt; LLM\n  RR -.-&gt; G\n  J -.-&gt; SYN\n  J -.-&gt; LLM\n  OUT --&gt; OBS\n</pre>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <span class=\"js-render-enrichment-loader d-flex flex-justify-center flex-items-center width-full\" style=\"min-height:100px\" role=\"presentation\">\n    <span data-view-component=\"true\">\n  <svg style=\"box-sizing: content-box; color: var(--color-icon-primary);\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" fill=\"none\" aria-hidden=\"true\" data-view-component=\"true\" class=\"octospinner mx-auto tmp-mx-auto anim-rotate\">\n    <circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"8\" r=\"7\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\"0.25\" stroke-width=\"2\" vector-effect=\"non-scaling-stroke\" fill=\"none\"></circle>\n    <path d=\"M15 8a7.002 7.002 0 00-7-7\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" vector-effect=\"non-scaling-stroke\"></path>\n</svg>    <span class=\"sr-only\">Loading</span>\n</span>\n  </span>\n</section>\n\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Web UI</h2><a id=\"user-content-web-ui\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Web UI\" href=\"#web-ui\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The web app (<code>web/</code>, served by nginx at <strong><a href=\"http://localhost:8080\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://localhost:8080</a></strong>) is built for\nchecking answers, not just reading them:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>the answer streams in while a step indicator shows the pipeline (plan,\nsearch, rank, weigh evidence, write) with the time each step took;</li>\n<li>every cited passage sits beside the answer with its file name, exact\ncharacter span, and the question's terms highlighted;</li>\n<li>with verification on, each answer sentence is underlined as supported or\nnot, links to its source, and the exact supporting sentence is highlighted\ninside that passage;</li>\n<li>confidence, risk of unsupported claims, and the evidence count sit under the\nanswer, and \"How this answer was produced\" lists the searches run, retriever\nresults, detected problems in plain language, and timings;</li>\n<li>Helpful / Not helpful feedback is tied to the exact answer (<code>query_id</code>);</li>\n<li>an Activity tab lists recent questions and feedback for your tenant;</li>\n<li>Settings holds the API address, an API key (kept for the browser tab only),\nyour user id, and the theme (light, dark, or system).</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It is plain HTML, CSS and ES modules with no build step. All server text is\ninserted as text nodes, and nginx sends a strict Content-Security-Policy. The\ntheme is light by default (dark is available in Settings), in the navy and\ngold of the SAG-RAG emblem.</p>\n<p align=\"center\" dir=\"auto\">\n  <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/atikulmunna/sagrag/HEAD/assets/sagrag-ui.png\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/atikulmunna/sagrag/HEAD/assets/sagrag-ui.png\" alt=\"SAG-RAG web UI: an answer about grief whose two sentences are each linked to the Seneca passage that supports them\" width=\"820\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a>\n</p>\n<p align=\"center\" dir=\"auto\"><em>Figure: a live answer from the local stack (qwen2.5:7b on Ollama, sentence verification on). Both sentences were checked against the cited passages of Seneca's Moral Letters; the supporting sentences are underlined in the margin and the query terms are highlighted.</em></p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">What it does</h2><a id=\"user-content-what-it-does\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: What it does\" href=\"#what-it-does\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>Speculative query planning.</strong> An LLM proposes an intent and alternative searches; the\noriginal question is always searched first and the plan is sanitized (the\nmodel cannot pick a domain or change policy). A rule-based plan from the\ndomain packs is the fallback.</li>\n<li><strong>Hybrid retrieval.</strong> Semantic (Qdrant) and keyword (Elasticsearch) search\nrun in parallel for every sub-query; table and key/value lines are pulled\nout of keyword hits; author-aware search runs when the question names an\nauthor.</li>\n<li><strong>Evidence processing.</strong> Policy and freshness filters, deduplication, author\nbias with gap-aware fallback, and a cross-encoder reranker.</li>\n<li><strong>Optional knowledge graph.</strong> Entities, claims, relations and heuristic\ncontradiction links in Neo4j feed the judge as extra signals.</li>\n<li><strong>Judge and synthesis.</strong> The judge picks trusted passages and a confidence;\nsynthesis writes a short answer. Prompts label evidence <code>E1</code>, <code>E2</code>, ... and\nrequest a JSON schema, so replies stay small enough for tight token limits\n(echoing 36-character chunk ids used to truncate them); a reply that is\nstill cut off keeps its complete sentences. Citations are validated against\nthe retrieved passages, and their source and offsets always come from the\nevidence, never from the model.</li>\n<li><strong>Sentence-level verification (opt-in).</strong> Each answer sentence is checked\nagainst the passages it cites with a small local NLI cross-encoder\n(sentence-sized premises, attribution phrases stripped, contradictions only\nfrom related sentences). The response marks every sentence supported,\nunsupported, or contradicted, and hallucination risk becomes the measured\nshare of unsupported sentences. Optionally the answer is withheld when too\nlittle of it is supported.</li>\n<li><strong>Graceful degradation.</strong> A missing service, a non-JSON model reply, or an\nunreachable Redis lowers quality but never takes the request path down, and\nevery degraded path is tagged and counted.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">How a query flows</h2><a id=\"user-content-how-a-query-flows\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: How a query flows\" href=\"#how-a-query-flows\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li>The client sends a question to <code>/v1/query</code> (or <code>/v1/query/stream</code>).</li>\n<li>The planner emits an intent and sub-queries.</li>\n<li>Each sub-query is embedded once (Redis-cached) and searched with the\nvector and keyword retrievers; structured lines come from the keyword hits.</li>\n<li>Author search runs when explicit author terms are detected.</li>\n<li>Results are filtered, deduplicated, author-biased, and reranked.</li>\n<li>The graph layer optionally adds entities, claims and relations.</li>\n<li>The judge validates evidence and sets a confidence.</li>\n<li>Synthesis returns the answer with validated provenance (falling back to\nformatted evidence on <code>non_json</code>, <code>timeout</code> or <code>error</code>), and verification\n(when enabled) checks each sentence against the cited passages.</li>\n<li>Failure tags, diagnostics, and latencies are recorded; the answer is\naudited under a fresh <code>query_id</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Quickstart (Docker Compose)</h2><a id=\"user-content-quickstart-docker-compose\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Quickstart (Docker Compose)\" href=\"#quickstart-docker-compose\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Prerequisites: Docker. For answers you also need an Ollama model, either\n<a href=\"https://ollama.com\" rel=\"nofollow\">Ollama</a> on the host or the bundled GPU container (below).</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"cp .env.example .env                 # placeholders only; edit as needed\npython tools/fetch_corpus.py         # public-domain Stoic texts -&gt; data/docs/stoicism\ncd infra\ndocker compose up -d --build         # add --profile llm for the Ollama container\ndocker compose exec ollama ollama pull qwen2.5:7b   # only with --profile llm\"><pre>cp .env.example .env                 <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> placeholders only; edit as needed</span>\npython tools/fetch_corpus.py         <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> public-domain Stoic texts -&gt; data/docs/stoicism</span>\n<span class=\"pl-c1\">cd</span> infra\ndocker compose up -d --build         <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> add --profile llm for the Ollama container</span>\ndocker compose <span class=\"pl-c1\">exec</span> ollama ollama pull qwen2.5:7b   <span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> only with --profile llm</span></pre></div>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Web UI: <a href=\"http://localhost:8080\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://localhost:8080</a></li>\n<li>API docs: <a href=\"http://localhost:8000/docs\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://localhost:8000/docs</a></li>\n<li>Readiness (which dependencies answer): <a href=\"http://localhost:8000/ready\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://localhost:8000/ready</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Documents live in <code>data/docs/&lt;domain&gt;/</code> as <code>.txt</code>, <code>.csv</code> or <code>.json</code> files\n(one folder per domain; file names starting with the author's name help\nauthor-aware retrieval). <code>tools/fetch_corpus.py</code> downloads Seneca's Moral\nLetters and Minor Dialogues, On Benefits, and Epictetus' Golden Sayings,\nstrips publisher boilerplate and translator notes, unwraps paragraphs, and\nwrites a <code>SOURCES.md</code> manifest. Ingest, then poll the job:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"curl -sS -X POST http://localhost:8000/v1/ingest\ncurl -sS http://localhost:8000/v1/ingest/&lt;job_id&gt;\"><pre>curl -sS -X POST http://localhost:8000/v1/ingest\ncurl -sS http://localhost:8000/v1/ingest/<span class=\"pl-k\">&lt;</span>job_id<span class=\"pl-k\">&gt;</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Compose reads <code>${...}</code> values from <code>infra/.env</code> (for example <code>HF_CACHE_DIR</code>,\nand <code>NEO4J_PASSWORD</code> when <code>GRAPH_ENABLED=true</code>; keep it equal to the one in\n<code>.env</code>). The <code>llm</code> profile runs <code>ollama/ollama</code> on an NVIDIA GPU and publishes\nport 11434, so the default <code>OLLAMA_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434</code>\nworks unchanged. <code>docker-compose.override.yml</code> (loaded automatically) mounts\n<code>app/</code> into the backend for development; run\n<code>docker compose -f docker-compose.yml up</code> for a production-like stack without\nthe mount. The backend image runs as a non-root user (uid 1000 by default; on\nLinux build with <code>--build-arg APP_UID=$(id -u)</code> if your <code>data/</code> directory is\nowned by another uid).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">To serve the UI from somewhere other than the bundled nginx, set\n<code>CORS_ORIGINS</code> to that origin and put the API address in the UI's Settings.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Configuration</h2><a id=\"user-content-configuration\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Configuration\" href=\"#configuration\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Every setting has a default in <code>app/config.py</code>; <a href=\".env.example\"><code>.env.example</code></a>\nshows the common ones with placeholder values.</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>LLM:</strong> <code>OLLAMA_URL</code>, <code>OLLAMA_MODEL</code>, <code>LLM_MAX_CONCURRENT</code>,\n<code>LLM_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_S</code>, <code>LLM_READ_TIMEOUT_S</code>, <code>SYNTHESIS_STREAM_TIMEOUT_S</code>,\n<code>JUDGE_TIMEOUT_S</code>, <code>SYNTHESIS_TIMEOUT_S</code>, <code>*_MAX_TOKENS</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Planner and retrieval:</strong> <code>PLANNER_MAX_QUERIES</code>, <code>RETRIEVER_TIMEOUT_S</code>,\n<code>RERANKER_TOP_K</code>, <code>RERANK_MAX_CANDIDATES</code> (default 40; candidates are chosen\nby reciprocal rank fusion across retrievers before the cross-encoder runs),\n<code>MAX_EVIDENCE_SNIPPETS</code>, <code>WARM_MODELS_ON_STARTUP</code> (default on: embedding,\nreranker and NLI models load in the background at startup).</li>\n<li><strong>Verification:</strong> <code>VERIFY_ENABLED</code> (default off; downloads a ~330 MB model on\nfirst use), <code>VERIFY_MODEL_NAME</code>, <code>VERIFY_MODEL_REVISION</code>, <code>VERIFY_THRESHOLD</code>\n(default 0.5), <code>VERIFY_TIMEOUT_S</code>, <code>ABSTAIN_BELOW_SUPPORT</code> (0 disables),\n<code>GRAPH_NLI_CONTRADICTIONS</code> (confirm graph contradictions with the same model).</li>\n<li><strong>Confidence calibration:</strong> <code>CONFIDENCE_ALIGNMENT_FLOOR</code> (default 0.55),\n<code>CONFIDENCE_ALIGNMENT_TOP_SCORE_MIN</code> (default -6.0), <code>MIN_RESULTS_COUNT</code>,\n<code>MIN_TOP_RERANK_SCORE</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Stores:</strong> <code>QDRANT_URL</code>, <code>ELASTIC_URL</code>, <code>NEO4J_URI</code>, <code>NEO4J_USER</code>,\n<code>NEO4J_PASSWORD</code>, <code>GRAPH_ENABLED</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Domains:</strong> <code>DOMAIN_KEYWORDS</code>, <code>DOMAIN_ALIASES</code>, <code>DOMAIN_MIN_KEYWORD_HITS</code>\n(default 2), <code>DOMAIN_FALLBACKS</code>, <code>DOMAIN_INDEX_MAP</code> (shared layout only),\n<code>DOMAIN_PACKS_PATH</code>, <code>QUERY_TERM_SYNONYMS</code>, <code>AUTHOR_INDEX_PATH</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Policy:</strong> <code>POLICY_BLOCKLIST</code>, <code>POLICY_ALLOWLIST</code>,\n<code>POLICY_SOURCE_TYPES_ALLOW/BLOCK</code>, <code>POLICY_DOMAINS_ALLOW/BLOCK</code>,\n<code>POLICY_RULES</code> (JSON list of <code>{action, domains, source_types, contains, not_contains}</code>; first match wins), <code>DEFAULT_FRESHNESS_DAYS</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Redis (best effort):</strong> <code>REDIS_URL</code>, <code>REDIS_RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED</code>,\n<code>REDIS_CACHE_ENABLED</code>, <code>QUERY_CACHE_TTL_S</code>, <code>EMBED_CACHE_TTL_S</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Auth, tenancy, rate limits:</strong> <code>AUTH_ENABLED</code>, <code>API_KEYS</code>, <code>API_KEY_MAP</code>,\n<code>TENANT_ISOLATION</code>, <code>RATE_LIMIT_PER_MINUTE</code>, <code>TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS</code>,\n<code>CORS_ORIGINS</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Exports:</strong> <code>AUDIT_EXPORT_PATH</code>, <code>LEARNING_EXPORT_PATH</code>,\n<code>LEARNING_MIN_RATING</code> (server-side paths; clients never choose them).</li>\n<li><strong>Observability:</strong> <code>OTEL_ENABLED</code>, <code>OTEL_SERVICE_NAME</code>,\n<code>OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h3 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Domain routing</h3><a id=\"user-content-domain-routing\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Domain routing\" href=\"#domain-routing\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"DOMAIN_KEYWORDS='{&quot;stoicism&quot;:[&quot;stoic&quot;,&quot;seneca&quot;,&quot;epictetus&quot;,&quot;marcus&quot;],&quot;finance&quot;:[&quot;earnings&quot;,&quot;revenue&quot;,&quot;sec&quot;]}'\nDOMAIN_MIN_KEYWORD_HITS=2\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code>DOMAIN_KEYWORDS='{\"stoicism\":[\"stoic\",\"seneca\",\"epictetus\",\"marcus\"],\"finance\":[\"earnings\",\"revenue\",\"sec\"]}'\nDOMAIN_MIN_KEYWORD_HITS=2\n</code></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Keywords match at word starts (\"stoic\" matches \"stoicism\", \"art\" does not\nmatch \"start\"). A client can pass <code>preferences.domain</code>, but only for a domain\nthat is configured or already ingested in its own namespace; anything else is\nrejected with 422. <code>GET /v1/domains</code> lists the valid values.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h3 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Author queries and fallback</h3><a id=\"user-content-author-queries-and-fallback\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Author queries and fallback\" href=\"#author-queries-and-fallback\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>If the question names an author (for example \"Seneca\"), results are biased\ntoward that author.</li>\n<li>Query terms are expanded with synonyms (for example \"fear\" to dread,\nterror, anxiety, timor, metus):\n<code>QUERY_TERM_SYNONYMS={\"fear\":[\"dread\",\"terror\",\"anxiety\",\"timor\",\"metus\"]}</code>.</li>\n<li>If no passage by that author mentions the query terms, the response says so\nand falls back to other sources (<code>author_gap</code>).</li>\n<li>Ingest maintains a lightweight author to source index to speed author\nfiltering.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Failure analysis</h2><a id=\"user-content-failure-analysis\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Failure analysis\" href=\"#failure-analysis\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Retrieval and synthesis problems are tagged on every response\n(<code>retrieval_failures</code>) and counted in <code>sag_rag_retrieval_failures_total</code>:\n<code>no_domain</code>, <code>policy_blocked</code>, <code>cross_domain_conflict</code>, <code>no_results</code>,\n<code>low_result_count</code>, <code>low_top_score</code>, <code>author_gap</code>,\n<code>vector|lexical|structured|lexical_author</code> + <code>_timeout|_error|_zero_hits</code>,\n<code>synthesis_timeout|synthesis_error</code>, and, with verification on,\n<code>unsupported_claims</code>, <code>contradicted_claims</code> and <code>abstained</code>. The streaming\nendpoint reports the same tags as the buffered one.</p>\n<section class=\"js-render-needs-enrichment render-needs-enrichment position-relative\" data-identity=\"d07de0c7-ae98-4608-a42d-1e44ddd7c0b8\" data-host=\"https://viewscreen.githubusercontent.com\" data-src=\"https://viewscreen.githubusercontent.com/markdown/mermaid?docs_host=https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.github.com\" data-type=\"mermaid\" aria-label=\"mermaid rendered output container\">\n  <div class=\"js-render-enrichment-target\" data-json=\"{&quot;data&quot;:&quot;flowchart LR\\n  Q[POST v1 query] --&gt; R[Retrieve and Rerank]\\n  R --&gt; S[Synthesis]\\n  S --&gt; O[Response]\\n\\n  R --&gt; RF[retrieval_failures tags]\\n  R --&gt; AD[agent_diagnostics]\\n  O --&gt; HR[hallucination_risk]\\n  O --&gt; EC[evidence_coverage]\\n  S --&gt; SO[sag_rag_synthesis_total]\\n  S --&gt; SL[sag_rag_synthesis_latency_ms_bucket]\\n  RF --&gt; M[GET metrics]\\n  AD --&gt; M\\n  HR --&gt; M\\n  EC --&gt; M\\n  SO --&gt; M\\n  SL --&gt; M\\n&quot;}\" data-plain=\"flowchart LR\n  Q[POST v1 query] --&gt; R[Retrieve and Rerank]\n  R --&gt; S[Synthesis]\n  S --&gt; O[Response]\n\n  R --&gt; RF[retrieval_failures tags]\n  R --&gt; AD[agent_diagnostics]\n  O --&gt; HR[hallucination_risk]\n  O --&gt; EC[evidence_coverage]\n  S --&gt; SO[sag_rag_synthesis_total]\n  S --&gt; SL[sag_rag_synthesis_latency_ms_bucket]\n  RF --&gt; M[GET metrics]\n  AD --&gt; M\n  HR --&gt; M\n  EC --&gt; M\n  SO --&gt; M\n  SL --&gt; M\n\" dir=\"auto\">\n    <div class=\"render-plaintext-hidden\" dir=\"auto\">\n      <pre lang=\"mermaid\" aria-label=\"Raw mermaid code\">flowchart LR\n  Q[POST v1 query] --&gt; R[Retrieve and Rerank]\n  R --&gt; S[Synthesis]\n  S --&gt; O[Response]\n\n  R --&gt; RF[retrieval_failures tags]\n  R --&gt; AD[agent_diagnostics]\n  O --&gt; HR[hallucination_risk]\n  O --&gt; EC[evidence_coverage]\n  S --&gt; SO[sag_rag_synthesis_total]\n  S --&gt; SL[sag_rag_synthesis_latency_ms_bucket]\n  RF --&gt; M[GET metrics]\n  AD --&gt; M\n  HR --&gt; M\n  EC --&gt; M\n  SO --&gt; M\n  SL --&gt; M\n</pre>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  <span class=\"js-render-enrichment-loader d-flex flex-justify-center flex-items-center width-full\" style=\"min-height:100px\" role=\"presentation\">\n    <span data-view-component=\"true\">\n  <svg style=\"box-sizing: content-box; color: var(--color-icon-primary);\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" fill=\"none\" aria-hidden=\"true\" data-view-component=\"true\" class=\"octospinner mx-auto tmp-mx-auto anim-rotate\">\n    <circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"8\" r=\"7\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-opacity=\"0.25\" stroke-width=\"2\" vector-effect=\"non-scaling-stroke\" fill=\"none\"></circle>\n    <path d=\"M15 8a7.002 7.002 0 00-7-7\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" vector-effect=\"non-scaling-stroke\"></path>\n</svg>    <span class=\"sr-only\">Loading</span>\n</span>\n  </span>\n</section>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">With verification on, <code>hallucination_risk</code> is the share of answer sentences\nthat no cited passage supports (<code>hallucination_risk_method: \"nli\"</code>) and\n<code>sag_rag_claims_total{status=...}</code> counts sentences by outcome. Without it, the\nscore falls back to the judge's confidence plus fixed penalties\n(<code>\"heuristic\"</code>), which is an estimate, not a measurement.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Observability</h2><a id=\"user-content-observability\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Observability\" href=\"#observability\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The backend exposes Prometheus text metrics at <code>/metrics</code> (and <code>/v1/metrics</code>):\nrequest counts and latency histograms (labelled by route template, so job ids\nand scanner URLs never create new series), retrieval failures, synthesis\noutcomes and latency, hallucination risk and evidence coverage. Histograms\ninclude <code>_sum</code> and <code>_count</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">An opt-in stack (Prometheus + Grafana + OpenTelemetry collector) ships behind a\nCompose profile so the core stack stays light:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"cd infra\ndocker compose --profile observability up\"><pre><span class=\"pl-c1\">cd</span> infra\ndocker compose --profile observability up</pre></div>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>Prometheus:</strong> <a href=\"http://localhost:9090\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://localhost:9090</a> (scrapes <code>backend:8000/metrics</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Grafana:</strong> <a href=\"http://localhost:3000\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://localhost:3000</a> (anonymous viewer enabled; admin/admin;\nlocal use only). A provisioned \"SAG-RAG Overview\" dashboard shows request\nrate and latency, retrieval failures, synthesis outcomes and p95 latency, and\nhallucination risk.</li>\n<li><strong>OTel collector:</strong> receives OTLP traces on <code>4317</code>/<code>4318</code>. Set\n<code>OTEL_ENABLED=true</code> (and <code>OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://otel-collector:4317</code>)\nso the backend exports spans; the collector logs them (add a Jaeger or Tempo\nexporter to visualize).</li>\n</ul>\n<p align=\"center\" dir=\"auto\">\n  <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/atikulmunna/sagrag/HEAD/assets/grafana-overview.png\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/atikulmunna/sagrag/HEAD/assets/grafana-overview.png\" alt=\"SAG-RAG Overview Grafana dashboard\" width=\"820\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a>\n</p>\n<p align=\"center\" dir=\"auto\"><em>Figure: the provisioned \"SAG-RAG Overview\" Grafana dashboard: request rate, latency p95, retrieval failures by tag, and synthesis outcomes, scraped live from <code>/metrics</code>.</em></p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Security</h2><a id=\"user-content-security\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Security\" href=\"#security\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Auth is <strong>opt-in</strong> so local development works without a key. For any\ndeployment beyond localhost, set:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"AUTH_ENABLED=true\nTENANT_ISOLATION=true\nAPI_KEY_MAP={&quot;prod-key-abc&quot;:&quot;acme&quot;,&quot;prod-key-def&quot;:&quot;globex&quot;}\n# or API_KEYS=key1,key2 (each gets a tenant id derived from a hash of the key)\"><pre>AUTH_ENABLED=true\nTENANT_ISOLATION=true\nAPI_KEY_MAP={<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>prod-key-abc<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>:<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>acme<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>,<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>prod-key-def<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>:<span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>globex<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>}\n<span class=\"pl-c\"><span class=\"pl-c\">#</span> or API_KEYS=key1,key2 (each gets a tenant id derived from a hash of the key)</span></pre></div>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Every endpoint requires <code>x-api-key</code> except <code>/health</code>, <code>/ready</code>, <code>/metrics</code>\nand the OpenAPI docs. Keys are compared in constant time; missing or unknown\nkeys get <code>401</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Tenant isolation is enforced server-side.</strong> The tenant comes from the key;\na body or query-string tenant is ignored for authenticated requests.\nStorage names keep tenants and domains apart (<code>docs_t_{tenant}</code> and\n<code>docs_t_{tenant}__d_{domain}</code>), names are validated slugs, and an isolated\nsearch never falls back to shared data. Audit rows, feedback, exports,\ningest job status, source deletion, and graph reads and writes are all\nscoped to the caller's tenant.</li>\n<li>Without auth, <code>TENANT_ISOLATION</code> uses the supplied tenant (or user id), so it\nis a convenience, not a security boundary; the backend logs a warning.</li>\n<li>The planner's output is untrusted: it cannot choose a domain or alter\npolicy, and synthesis output cannot add or overwrite response fields.</li>\n<li>Exports (<code>/v1/audit/export</code>, <code>/v1/learning/export</code>) return NDJSON downloads\nor write to server-configured paths; a client-supplied <code>path</code> is rejected.</li>\n<li>Rate limits key on the tenant when authenticated, otherwise on the client\naddress; <code>X-Forwarded-For</code> is only trusted for <code>TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS</code> proxies.</li>\n<li>The web container sends a strict CSP and renders all server text as text.</li>\n<li><code>.env</code> and <code>infra/.env</code> are git-ignored; never commit real keys. Provide them\nthrough the environment or a secret store (for Compose, an injected env file\nor Docker secrets), not baked into images.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">API reference</h2><a id=\"user-content-api-reference\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: API reference\" href=\"#api-reference\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The always-current schema (request and response models included) is at\n<code>/docs</code>, <code>/redoc</code> and <code>/openapi.json</code>. Highlights:</p>\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Method</th>\n<th>Path</th>\n<th>Purpose</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>POST</td>\n<td><code>/v1/query</code></td>\n<td>Buffered answer + provenance + diagnostics (cached)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>POST</td>\n<td><code>/v1/query/stream</code></td>\n<td>SSE: <code>stage</code>, <code>meta</code>, <code>token</code>, <code>final</code> (same body as <code>/v1/query</code>), <code>error</code>, <code>done</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>GET</td>\n<td><code>/v1/domains</code></td>\n<td>Domains valid for <code>preferences.domain</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>POST</td>\n<td><code>/v1/ingest</code></td>\n<td>Start a background ingest job (202, <code>{job_id}</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>GET</td>\n<td><code>/v1/ingest/{job_id}</code></td>\n<td>Job status: <code>queued</code>, <code>running</code>, <code>succeeded</code>, <code>completed_with_errors</code>, <code>failed</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>DELETE</td>\n<td><code>/v1/ingest/source/{source}</code></td>\n<td>Delete a source from the caller's namespaces</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>GET</td>\n<td><code>/v1/audit</code></td>\n<td>Recent queries (cursor paging)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>POST</td>\n<td><code>/v1/audit/export</code></td>\n<td>NDJSON download, or <code>{\"save\": true}</code> to the configured path</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>POST</td>\n<td><code>/v1/feedback</code></td>\n<td>Rating 1 to 5, optional comment and <code>query_id</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>GET</td>\n<td><code>/v1/feedback/list</code></td>\n<td>Recent feedback</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>POST</td>\n<td><code>/v1/learning/export</code></td>\n<td>Interactions rated at or above <code>min_rating</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>POST</td>\n<td><code>/v1/graph/summary</code></td>\n<td>Graph reasoning for chunk ids</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>GET</td>\n<td><code>/health</code>, <code>/ready</code>, <code>/metrics</code></td>\n<td>Liveness, dependency readiness, Prometheus</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Endpoints are also mounted at the root (<code>/query</code>, ...) for backwards\ncompatibility.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Evaluation</h2><a id=\"user-content-evaluation\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Evaluation\" href=\"#evaluation\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">A small labeled query set lives in <code>data/eval/queries.jsonl</code>. Score a running\nstack with:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"python tools/ablation_eval.py --base-urls http://localhost:8000 \\\n  --queries data/eval/queries.jsonl --output ablation_results.jsonl \\\n  --score --ground-truth data/eval/queries.jsonl --k 5\"><pre>python tools/ablation_eval.py --base-urls http://localhost:8000 \\\n  --queries data/eval/queries.jsonl --output ablation_results.jsonl \\\n  --score --ground-truth data/eval/queries.jsonl --k 5</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This produces retrieval recall@k / hit rate and answer-quality scores\n(LLM-judge faithfulness plus a lexical-overlap baseline). See\n<a href=\"data/eval/README.md\"><code>data/eval/README.md</code></a>. The set has six single-domain\nquestions, so scores are indicative only; no benchmark numbers are published\nyet.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The verifier has its own sanity check: <code>python tools/verify_eval.py</code> runs the\nreal NLI model over hand-labeled claims in <code>data/eval/nli_cases.jsonl</code>\n(currently 11 of 12 correct; the miss is a loose paraphrase it conservatively\nmarks unsupported). Twelve cases is a smoke test, not a benchmark.</p>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Upgrading from earlier versions</h2><a id=\"user-content-upgrading-from-earlier-versions\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Upgrading from earlier versions\" href=\"#upgrading-from-earlier-versions\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>Re-ingest your documents.</strong> Character offsets were computed incorrectly\nbefore (cited spans drifted), chunk ids now include the namespace, and graph\nnodes now carry a tenant key.</li>\n<li>With <code>TENANT_ISOLATION=true</code>, data moves to <code>docs_t_{tenant}...</code> names; a key\nin <code>API_KEYS</code> without an <code>API_KEY_MAP</code> entry now maps to a hash-derived\ntenant instead of the raw key.</li>\n<li>The Gradio app is replaced by the web UI on port 8080, and the backend's\n<code>/ui</code> page is removed.</li>\n<li>Export endpoints no longer accept <code>path</code>; feedback ratings must be 1 to 5;\n<code>preferences.domain</code> must be a known domain.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">How it differs from other RAG approaches</h2><a id=\"user-content-how-it-differs-from-other-rag-approaches\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: How it differs from other RAG approaches\" href=\"#how-it-differs-from-other-rag-approaches\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">These are design intentions; they have not been benchmarked against the\nalternatives yet.</p>\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Technique</th>\n<th>Strengths</th>\n<th>Limitations</th>\n<th>What SAG-RAG adds</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Naive RAG (single retriever, no planning)</td>\n<td>Simple, fast to build</td>\n<td>Irrelevant context, weaker grounding</td>\n<td>Planned sub-queries and parallel retrievers</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Vector-only RAG</td>\n<td>Semantic similarity</td>\n<td>Misses exact matches, brittle for numbers</td>\n<td>Keyword and structured retrieval plus reranking</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>BM25-only RAG</td>\n<td>Exact-match recall</td>\n<td>Poor semantic coverage</td>\n<td>Embeddings and query planning</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Hybrid RAG (vector + BM25)</td>\n<td>Better recall</td>\n<td>Still noisy; limited verification</td>\n<td>Judge, validated provenance, optional graph signals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Rerank-only pipelines</td>\n<td>Higher relevance</td>\n<td>No verification</td>\n<td>Explicit judge and contradiction signals</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Graph-RAG (entity graph)</td>\n<td>Explainability</td>\n<td>Shallow reasoning</td>\n<td>Claims, relation and contradiction signals for the judge</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Toolformer-style agentic RAG</td>\n<td>Flexible tool use</td>\n<td>Hard to audit</td>\n<td>Fixed, observable stages with audit logs</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\n<div class=\"markdown-heading\" dir=\"auto\"><h2 class=\"heading-element\" dir=\"auto\">Known limitations</h2><a id=\"user-content-known-limitations\" class=\"anchor\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Known limitations\" href=\"#known-limitations\"><svg data-component=\"Octicon\" class=\"octicon octicon-link\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m7.775 3.275 1.25-1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1 4.95 4.95l-2.5 2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1 .018-1.042.751.751 0 0 1 1.042-.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l2.5-2.5a2.002 2.002 0 0 0-2.83-2.83l-1.25 1.25a.751.751 0 0 1-1.042-.018.751.751 0 0 1-.018-1.042Zm-4.69 9.64a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 2.83 0l1.25-1.25a.751.751 0 0 1 1.042.018.751.751 0 0 1 .018 1.042l-1.25 1.25a3.5 3.5 0 1 1-4.95-4.95l2.5-2.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 4.95 0 .751.751 0 0 1-.018 1.042.751.751 0 0 1-1.042.018 1.998 1.998 0 0 0-2.83 0l-2.5 2.5a1.998 1.998 0 0 0 0 2.83Z\"></path></svg></a></div>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><strong>Confidence is uncalibrated.</strong> It comes from the judge model plus graph\npenalties and an alignment floor. Hallucination risk is only measured when\nverification is on; otherwise it is derived from that confidence.</li>\n<li><strong>Verification is a small model.</strong> It cannot read support that a source\nexpresses as a rhetorical question (\"what is baser than to chase after\npleasure in mourning?\"), so such sentences may show as unsupported; questions\nare never allowed to count as contradictions. It checks sentences only\nagainst the passages the answer cites and adds latency (about 1.5 seconds for a\nfour-sentence answer over three passages on a 16-thread desktop CPU; the\nmodel is warmed up at startup). It has only been sanity-checked on twelve\nlabeled claims.</li>\n<li><strong>Graph contradictions are partly heuristic.</strong> Candidates are similar\nsentences about a shared entity; they are confirmed by NLI when\n<code>GRAPH_NLI_CONTRADICTIONS</code> is on, otherwise by opposite negation. Relation\nconflicts are differing predicates for one entity pair.</li>\n<li><strong>Evaluation scope.</strong> The bundled eval set is small and single-domain.</li>\n<li><strong>Answers vary between runs.</strong> GPU inference is not fully deterministic\neven at temperature 0, so the same question can produce differently worded\nanswers (and verification results).</li>\n<li><strong>Single-node infra.</strong> Qdrant, Elasticsearch, Neo4j and Redis run\nsingle-node via Compose. Redis is best effort; the ingest worker is\nin-process (one job at a time per process), not a distributed consumer.</li>\n<li><strong>Training.</strong> LoRA or fine-tuning is out of scope; <code>learning/export</code> only\nemits highly rated interactions.</li>\n<li><strong>Route duplication.</strong> Endpoints are mounted at both <code>/v1/*</code> and <code>/*</code> for\ncompatibility.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See <a href=\"docs/architecture.md#known-limitations\"><code>docs/architecture.md</code></a> for details.</p>\n</article></div>";
